@startuml publication
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Configurable publication and completion
caption Delivery mode is explicit: PR with human review, PR without it, or direct push to main.

state Entry <<choice>>
state "Reconcile interrupted delivery\nRead remote PR/main and task status\nMatch saved operation + approved snapshot" as Recover
state "Verify publication prerequisites\nCurrent task/spec/policy; internally approved snapshot\nRequired checks and branch/base identity" as Verify
state DeliveryMode <<choice>>
state "Push reviewed branch\nVerify exact remote commit\nReconcile retries by operation ID" as Push
state "Create or update PR\nVerify PR identity and head commit" as PR
state ReviewTracking <<choice>>
state "Update Jira: PR published\nLink PR, commit, checks and agent review\nVerify configured status + ticket update" as InReview
state "Update prompt task: PR published\nLink PR, commit, checks and agent review\nVerify task update" as PromptInReview
state ReviewMode <<choice>>
state "Request human review\nPR review or task chat prompt\nInclude PR and exact commit" as Request
state "Await human decision\nEnd run; release slot and agent sessions" as Awaiting <<attention>>
state "Ingest human response\nAuthenticate actor; record PR/chat source\nBind decision + feedback to PR head" as HumanResponse
state HumanDecision <<choice>>
state "Validate renewed human approval\nCurrent task spec/policy, PR head + base\nSenior approval + required checks bind exact snapshot" as ResumeGate
state "Return actionable feedback\nIn-scope repair; invalidate old approvals\nRevalidate; repeat configured reviews" as Repair <<attention>>
state "PR completion gate\nHuman approval if configured\nCurrent head, checks, policy and base" as Gate
state "Reconcile branch with current base\nChanged snapshot requires new checks\nand configured reviews" as Rebase
state "Merge PR or verify external merge\nConfirm exact target and merged commit" as Merge
state "Direct-main gate\nAgent-approved snapshot, current main head\nChecks, policy and push permission" as DirectGate
state "Push directly to main\nFast-forward only; no force push\nVerify exact remote main commit" as DirectPush
state CompletionTarget <<choice>>
state "Update Jira: Done\nLink published commit + PR if any + evidence\nVerify status and ticket revision" as Done
state "Mark prompt-only task complete\nRecord published commit + review evidence\nVerify internal task status" as PromptDone
state "Task complete\nTarget branch + completion verified\nJira Done when linked" as Complete <<success>>
state "Needs attention\nFinal rejection, ambiguity, or failed recovery" as Attention <<attention>>
state "Scope blocker\nPreserve work and create/link prerequisite" as ScopeBlock <<blocked>>

[*] --> Entry
Entry --> Verify : [new internally approved code]
Entry --> HumanResponse : [human response for published PR]
Entry --> Recover : [delivery recovery pending]
Recover --> CompletionTarget : target branch update verified; completion pending
Recover --> Verify : no remote publication; approved snapshot still current
Recover --> Attention : external result remains ambiguous
Verify --> DeliveryMode : snapshot and permissions current
Verify --> Repair : code/base changed
Verify --> Attention : scope/spec/policy requires reassessment
DeliveryMode --> Push : [pr_human or pr_automatic]
DeliveryMode --> DirectGate : [direct_main]
Push --> PR : remote head verified
PR --> ReviewTracking : PR head verified
ReviewTracking --> InReview : [Jira ticket linked]
ReviewTracking --> PromptInReview : [prompt-only; no ticket]
InReview --> ReviewMode : Jira update confirmed
PromptInReview --> ReviewMode : task update confirmed
ReviewMode --> Request : [pr_human]
ReviewMode --> Gate : [pr_automatic]
Request --> Awaiting : review request recorded
HumanResponse --> HumanDecision : actor, task, PR and head verified
HumanResponse --> Attention : identity or binding ambiguous
HumanDecision --> Repair : [changes requested or repairable denial]
HumanDecision --> ResumeGate : [approved]
HumanDecision --> ScopeBlock : [confirmed necessary scope expansion]
HumanDecision --> Attention : [final rejection or unresolved decision]
ResumeGate --> Gate : all identities, approval and checks current
ResumeGate --> Repair : code/spec/checks or senior approval stale\n/ invalidate old approvals; renew review
ResumeGate --> Attention : identity or policy binding ambiguous
Gate --> Merge : required approvals, checks and target current
Gate --> Rebase : base moved / reconcile
Gate --> Awaiting : [pr_human; platform approval missing] / re-request
Gate --> Attention : [pr_automatic; host requires human]\nor policy denial/conflict
Rebase --> Repair : new snapshot / invalidate approvals
Merge --> CompletionTarget : remote merge verified
DirectGate --> DirectPush : expected main head + policy current
DirectGate --> Repair : main moved / revalidate final snapshot
DirectGate --> Repair : integration changed reviewed snapshot
DirectGate --> Attention : push permission or protection denied
DirectPush --> CompletionTarget : remote main head verified
DirectPush --> Repair : main moved before push / revalidate
DirectPush --> Attention : remote effect uncertain after recovery
CompletionTarget --> Done : [Jira ticket linked]
CompletionTarget --> PromptDone : [prompt-only; no ticket]
Done --> Complete : Jira Done verified
Done --> Attention : Jira update unconfirmed after recovery
PromptDone --> Complete : task completion verified
PromptDone --> Attention : task update unconfirmed after recovery
Awaiting --> [*] : return awaiting_review
Complete --> [*] : return complete
Repair --> [*] : return repair_required
Attention --> [*] : return attention
ScopeBlock --> [*] : return scope_blocked

note right of HumanResponse
  PR comments and task chat replies are normalized
  into one observable human-review record.
  A chat approval does not bypass a PR host's
  required approval rules.
end note
note right of ResumeGate
  Human-response intake occurs in a NEW run after preflight.
  Preflight routes in-scope feedback to implementation first.
  This gate independently rechecks the current task specification,
  reviewed snapshot and PR head immediately before merge.
  After repair, publication updates the PR and requests human review again.
end note
note right of DirectGate
  Concurrent tasks serialize integration with main.
  If main changes, repeat validation and senior review
  for the exact code that would be pushed.
  No implicit fallback to a PR or force push.
end note
note bottom of Awaiting
  The task remains pending. The next authenticated human response
  queues a NEW run, which repeats ticket/code preflight.
end note
note bottom of Done
  Branch push, PR, merge, direct push and Jira mutations use operation-guardrails.puml.
  Reconcile uncertain remote outcomes before retrying.
  Failure to update Jira leaves the task incomplete and recoverable.
end note
@enduml
